I understand that subset.cross() is effective for pulling out specific SNPs or specific individuals, but is there a way to subset specific phenotypes in a cross object? Thanks.

From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Tue Jan  9 03:02:02 2018
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Tue, 09 Jan 2018 03:02:02 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] subset phenotypes
Message-ID: <Ew0hwSu1nXY.IVLdF0UrEAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <Ew0hwSu1nXY.n2iUvr7bAAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <Ew0hwSu1nXY.n2iUvr7bAAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/Ew0hwSu1nXY/m/IVLdF0UrEAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A cross object is a list; the phenotypes are in a component named "pheno", as a data frame.

To subset columns of the phenotypes, use something like:

  mycross$pheno <- mycross$pheno[, c(1,3,5)]

karl

